From 4201408d919f9787af43a075068947a44e95a231 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronny Stiftel <ronny.stiftel@tomcom.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:31:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Persist opt-in invasion victory rewards outside the invaded
 world

Reward joined victories through server-owned TradeDesk grants: one Insight plus
policy Echoes for the defending host, or the solo invader when the victim reports
killed_by_invader. Retire the invasion before paying, freeze defeated levels and
exclude cancellations, environmental deaths, boss/timeout/disconnect and wipes.

Use a durable per-authenticated-player reward mailbox, because solo invaders send
no party Hello. High-bit grant IDs route acknowledgements separately from party
trades; pending payments, counters and acknowledgements survive server restart.
LobbyHello capability negotiation preserves compatibility with original clients.

Reject unknown/server-only item kinds in ordinary refunds and malformed grants
before application. Add service tests covering true solo winners, duplicate ends,
legacy reconnects, stolen acknowledgements, pending grants and durable counters.

The Echoes polynomial is an explicit bounded server policy, not a retail-exact
claim for all levels/covenants. Native game reward validation is separate work.

Validation: isolated opc ARM64 Docker image build and 10/10 focused CTest suites
passed, including bloodborne_world, bloodborne_trade and world_writer. The live
Bloodborne service, its data/config/identity and unrelated containers were not
replaced or restarted by this commit.

