@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Invasion reward deployment on opc
+
+This recipe extends the owner's existing ARM64 deployment. It changes the Bloodborne service
+only and leaves `/data`, account identities, saves, configuration and unrelated containers in
+place. Do not overwrite the original rollback image `bloodborne-server:8d5e54f-arm64`.
+
+## Source and build
+
+The review branch is `codex/invasion-victory-rewards`, based on
+`8d5e54fee50e1d7c9dd25ba0a32f224b1d76b6f1` in the original
+[lKaniel/bloodborne-server](https://github.com/lKaniel/bloodborne-server) repository.
+Original authors: Kaniel / lKaniel, Vitalii Shevchuk (source history), and the shadNet Project
+contributors (original SPDX holders). Their existing server, trade, stream and world-store code
+is retained under GPL-2.0-or-later.
+
+Use a separate worktree, for example `/docker/bloodborne-server/invasion-rewards-source`.
+Initialize `server/externals/protobuf` from the pinned submodule. Retain the local ARM64 build
+recipe from the existing `source/server/hosting/Dockerfile.opc` and its dockerignore in this
+worktree as `server/hosting/Dockerfile.rewards` and `.dockerignore`. The original hosting files
+are local deployment configuration and are not part of this source commit.
+
+Add `test_bloodborne_world test_world_writer` to that recipe's test build targets, and
+`bloodborne_world|world_writer` to its focused ctest expression, alongside the existing
+server_link/build_fingerprint/packet_routes/rpc_tunnel/admission/http_gate/team_lobby/trade tests.
+
+```sh
+docker build --build-arg BUILD_JOBS=4 \
+  --build-arg SOURCE_REVISION=8d5e54fee50e1d7c9dd25ba0a32f224b1d76b6f1 \
+  -f server/hosting/Dockerfile.rewards \
+  -t bloodborne-server:invasion-rewards-test-arm64 .
+```
+
+Keep the native protocol admission revision pinned for compatibility with the matching original
+client/core source; the append-only reward capability gates the extension. Record this source
+patch commit separately in the deployment log/image tag. There is no global protocol increment
+and no configuration change to the invasion enable/kind/sign settings in this server patch.
+
+The Docker build executes the focused tests before producing the image. The new checks cover
+both winners, non-reward endings, repeated death reports, frozen levels, real solo players with
+no party Hello, pending mailbox restart, legacy reconnect, ACK persistence, another authenticated
+identity's forged ACK, server-only item/refund rejection and malformed grant validation.
+
+## Service replacement and validation
+
+Before replacing the service, record its current compose service name, image reference and
+health status. Save an exact copy of `/docker/docker-compose.yaml`. Update only the Bloodborne
+image value to the new image, then recreate only that service with its existing volumes and
+configuration; no volume removal or account reset is required. Preserve the previous image and
+compose copy for rollback. Test capable and original clients, then verify the service is healthy.
+
+The client must set `LobbyHello.invasion_rewards=true`, implement the exact reward shape in
+`docs/INVASIONS.md`, and acknowledge the high-bit grant only after applying it. The original
+client does not advertise this capability and receives no reward extension. No new firewall
+ports are needed. A meaningful in-game test must show one Insight and the expected Echoes for
+both defending and invading victories, no double native payment, and no reward for cancellation
+or an environmental host death. Unit tests alone do not establish those in-game results.
